<title>ZAIRE: Zaire's rebel leader flies to Kisangani.</title>
<headline>Zaire's rebel leader flies to Kisangani.</headline>
<dateline>GOMA, Zaire 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zairean rebel leader Laurent Kabila flew to the newly captured city of Kisangani on Friday but made no comment on a call by ailing President Mobutu Sese Seko for a truce, witnesses said.</p>
<p>Kabila, head of the Alliance of Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Congo-Zaire (ADFL), was to address a rally in Zaire's third largest city and hold talks later with United Nations special envoy Mohamed Sahnoun.</p>
